    "created_at": "2016-06-08T23:23:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-08T23:23:16Z",
    "body": "Yes. It's what was (intentionally!) used for `<style scoped>`, and if you use a relative selector (like .query()), it gets taken care of automatically (you'll only ever select the scoping element if you do it on purpose).\n\nIt's just this case, with an absolute selector that still wants to act kinda like a relative selector, that's problematic.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
